---
/** How precisely the Great Pyramid faces north, and two proposed methods. */
import Level from './Level.astro';
import Cite from './Cite.astro';
---

<figure class="align">
  <div class="panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 220 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="al-t1">
      <title id="al-t1">The base and true north</title>
      <line class="north" x1="110" y1="12" x2="110" y2="208" />
      <text x="116" y="22" class="n">True north</text>
      <g transform="rotate(-3 110 115)">
        <rect class="base" x="45" y="50" width="130" height="130" />
      </g>
      <text x="110" y="200" class="c">Error exaggerated about 50×</text>
    </svg>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 220 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="al-t2">
      <title id="al-t2">Star method: a plumb line and two stars</title>
      <circle class="star" cx="80" cy="40" r="4" />
      <circle class="star" cx="140" cy="150" r="4" />
      <text x="88" y="36" class="n">star A</text>
      <text x="148" y="154" class="n">star B</text>
      <line class="plumb" x1="110" y1="20" x2="110" y2="200" />
      <line class="ghostline" x1="80" y1="40" x2="140" y2="150" />
      <text x="110" y="212" class="c">When both stars line up on a plumb line</text>
    </svg>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 220 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="al-t3">
      <title id="al-t3">Sun method: the tip of a shadow on the equinox</title>
      <line class="ground" x1="10" y1="160" x2="210" y2="160" />
      <line class="gnomon" x1="110" y1="160" x2="110" y2="95" />
      <path class="shadow" d="M40,185 Q110,176 180,185" />
      {[45, 75, 110, 145, 175].map((x) => <circle class="tip" cx={x} cy={180 + Math.abs(x - 110) * 0.06} r="3" />)}
      <text x="110" y="208" class="c">Shadow tips mark an east–west line</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <Level level="established" /> <span>Petrie measured the sides as turned on average only about 3′43″ (under a tenth of a degree) from true north. <Cite ids={['petrie']} /></span>
    <Level level="debated" /> <span>How it was done is debated. Kate Spence proposed using the simultaneous transit of two stars across a plumb line, which would also explain the small errors (2000). Glen Dash proposed marking the tips of a gnomon's shadow around the equinox (2017). <Cite ids={['spence', 'dash']} /> The diagrams are schematic; the stars are not drawn in their real positions.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .align { margin: 0; }
  .panels { display: grid; gap: 0.8rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(11rem, 1fr)); }
  svg { width: 100%; height: auto; background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 30%, #231d14, #0d0b08 85%); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  .north { stroke: #f0b73a; stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .base { fill: rgb(216 203 168 / 0.25); stroke: #e9e0c8; stroke-width: 2; }
  .n { fill: #d8cba8; font: 10px var(--font-body); }
  .c { fill: #bfb297; font: 10px var(--font-body); text-anchor: middle; }
  .star { fill: #fff2cc; }
  .plumb { stroke: #e9e0c8; stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .ghostline { stroke: #7fa7d9; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; }
  .ground { stroke: #7a6f58; }
  .gnomon { stroke: #e9e0c8; stroke-width: 3; }
  .shadow { fill: none; stroke: #7fa7d9; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; }
  .tip { fill: #f0b73a; }
  figcaption { margin-top: 0.7rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 0.5rem 0.7rem; align-items: start; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 85ch; }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) { figcaption { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
